<a name="toc_tc63599"></a><p>&nbsp;</p><div> <table class="tc" width="90%" ><tr><th colspan="4">Test Case CTCP-4112: Verify QR code scanning functionality in case Conti+ app is intalled  but user not have access of HE&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 80%;">[Version  : 1]</span></th></tr>
<tr><td width="20%" valign="top"><span class="label">Author:</span></td><td colspan="3">uie_32437</td></tr>
<tr><td colspan="4"><span class="label">Summary:</span><br /><p>Verify QR code scanning functionality in case Conti+ app is intalled &nbsp;but user not have access of HE</p>
</td></tr><tr><td colspan="4"><span class="label">Preconditions:</span><br /><p>User do not have access of HE module via permission and assignment screen</p>
</td></tr><tr><td><span class="label">#:</span></td><td><span class="label">Step actions:</span></td><td><span class="label">Expected Results:</span></td></tr><tr><td width="5">1</td><td><p>Scan the QR code&nbsp;</p>
</td><td><p>If Conti+ 2.0 App installed on phone and user has&nbsp;<strong>not</strong>&nbsp;required assignment and permission to access object, show &quot;Access denied&quot; in Conti+ 2.0 App</p>
</td></tr><tr><td width="5">2</td><td><p>Scan the QR code&nbsp;</p>
</td><td><p>If Conti+ 2.0 App installed on phone and user has&nbsp;<strong>not</strong>&nbsp;required assignment and permission to access object, show &quot;Access denied&quot; in Conti+ 2.0 App</p>
